1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:12,160
If working hard were enough to make you rich, the people who open the market stalls before dawn and work late into the night in tough conditions would be the richest people in the world.

2
00:00:12,710 --> 00:00:13,790
But they're not.

3
00:00:14,340 --> 00:00:16,572
It's not that they don't work hard enough.

4
00:00:16,772 --> 00:00:19,112
They work harder than almost anyone.

5
00:00:19,312 --> 00:00:23,848
Which means wealth isn't decided by effort alone.

6
00:00:24,398 --> 00:00:29,114
People who work hard but never become wealthy tend to have something in common.

7
00:00:29,314 --> 00:00:32,806
Today, I'll share four things they share.

8
00:00:33,356 --> 00:00:37,496
And I'll show you how what you want actually comes to you.

9
00:00:37,696 --> 00:00:40,144
It's probably the opposite of what you think.

10
00:00:40,344 --> 00:00:45,744
Along with the story of a piece of paper an unknown actor named Jim Carrey kept in his wallet.

11
00:00:46,894 --> 00:00:48,982
First, you need to know this.

12
00:00:49,182 --> 00:00:55,446
In Korean saju, the Four Pillars of Destiny, it's said that everyone has a vessel for wealth.

13
00:00:55,646 --> 00:01:00,362
When more money comes in than the vessel can hold, it overflows and drains away.

14
00:01:00,912 --> 00:01:03,684
There's a study of lottery winners in Florida.

15
00:01:03,884 --> 00:01:14,324
People who won fifty to a hundred and fifty thousand dollars were, a few years later, going bankrupt at about the same rate as people who'd won very little.

16
00:01:14,874 --> 00:01:16,170
The money came in.

17
00:01:16,369 --> 00:01:18,133
But the vessel stayed the same.

18
00:01:18,684 --> 00:01:24,336
Spiritually, your vessel is as big as what you feel you're able to receive.

19
00:01:24,536 --> 00:01:27,884
People who work hard but never get ahead have a blocked vessel.

20
00:01:28,084 --> 00:01:29,596
So what's blocking it?

21
00:01:30,746 --> 00:01:32,186
The first thing they share.

22
00:01:32,386 --> 00:01:34,833
Believing that having less is a virtue.

23
00:01:35,033 --> 00:01:37,014
Don't be greedy about money.

24
00:01:37,214 --> 00:01:38,870
Money changes people.

25
00:01:39,070 --> 00:01:43,029
As long as you're at peace, it doesn't matter if you have little.

26
00:01:43,229 --> 00:01:45,533
We've heard these since we were kids.

27
00:01:46,083 --> 00:01:48,892
So we accept going without as normal.

28
00:01:49,091 --> 00:01:52,511
We even think having less is humble, or good.

29
00:01:52,711 --> 00:01:56,455
And saying what we want starts to feel like greed.

30
00:01:57,005 --> 00:02:03,701
If you want money but also think money is bad, you're calling it with one hand and pushing it away with the other.

31
00:02:03,901 --> 00:02:06,457
Having less is not a virtue.

32
00:02:06,657 --> 00:02:08,386
It's just one experience.

33
00:02:08,585 --> 00:02:11,646
It's okay to want abundance.

34
00:02:11,845 --> 00:02:14,402
That's the belief that has to change first.

35
00:02:14,951 --> 00:02:16,391
The second thing they share.

36
00:02:16,591 --> 00:02:18,283
Not knowing how to receive.

37
00:02:18,483 --> 00:02:22,803
Someone compliments you, and you say, oh no, not really.

38
00:02:23,003 --> 00:02:26,315
Someone offers help, and you say, I'm fine.

39
00:02:26,515 --> 00:02:29,287
Someone gives you a gift, and you feel guilty.

40
00:02:29,487 --> 00:02:34,131
If you only give and never receive, the flow gets blocked.

41
00:02:34,331 --> 00:02:37,931
Energy has to come in and go out to keep moving.

42
00:02:38,481 --> 00:02:39,993
The third thing they share.

43
00:02:40,193 --> 00:02:41,849
The vibration of lack.

44
00:02:42,049 --> 00:02:43,237
I don't have enough.

45
00:02:43,437 --> 00:02:44,625
It's never enough.

46
00:02:44,825 --> 00:02:49,145
When you want money from that feeling, the feeling of not having just keeps going.

47
00:02:50,295 --> 00:02:51,303
And the fourth.

48
00:02:51,503 --> 00:02:53,699
This is the trap most people fall into.

49
00:02:53,899 --> 00:02:57,355
Especially people who search for videos like this one.

50
00:02:57,905 --> 00:02:59,345
I am rich.

51
00:02:59,545 --> 00:03:01,309
Money comes easily to me.

52
00:03:01,509 --> 00:03:02,985
You say it every day.

53
00:03:03,535 --> 00:03:07,999
But if you're saying it out loud while not believing a word of it inside, it does nothing.

54
00:03:08,549 --> 00:03:12,761
The harder you force yourself to believe, the emptier you feel.

55
00:03:12,961 --> 00:03:16,057
Because nothing has actually changed.

56
00:03:16,257 --> 00:03:22,449
And eventually you think, see, it doesn't work, and you see the world even more darkly.

57
00:03:22,999 --> 00:03:26,095
The problem was never a lack of belief.

58
00:03:26,295 --> 00:03:29,355
The problem was that you were forcing it.

59
00:03:30,505 --> 00:03:31,981
So what do you do instead?

60
00:03:32,181 --> 00:03:36,393
Not force yourself to believe, but imagine, joyfully.

61
00:03:36,943 --> 00:03:43,711
When Jim Carrey was still unknown, he'd reportedly drive out alone at night and imagine directors wanting to work with him.

62
00:03:43,911 --> 00:03:45,243
It made him feel good.

63
00:03:45,443 --> 00:03:49,439
Then he wrote himself a check for ten million dollars.

64
00:03:49,639 --> 00:03:51,547
For acting services rendered.

65
00:03:51,747 --> 00:03:55,959
He dated it Thanksgiving, a few years in the future, and kept it in his wallet.

66
00:03:56,509 --> 00:04:01,693
And around that Thanksgiving, he found out he'd be paid ten million dollars for a movie.

67
00:04:02,243 --> 00:04:04,223
But there's something he always adds.

68
00:04:04,423 --> 00:04:07,843
You can't just visualize, and then go eat a sandwich.

69
00:04:08,393 --> 00:04:12,857
Whatever it is you want, picture yourself already having it.

70
00:04:13,057 --> 00:04:14,101
How would you feel?

71
00:04:14,301 --> 00:04:15,993
How would you spend your day?

72
00:04:16,193 --> 00:04:18,749
Who would you talk to, and about what?

73
00:04:18,949 --> 00:04:21,937
If you bought a home, how would you decorate it?

74
00:04:22,487 --> 00:04:23,351
Lightly.

75
00:04:23,551 --> 00:04:24,487
Joyfully.

76
00:04:24,688 --> 00:04:25,479
Often.

77
00:04:25,680 --> 00:04:31,764
So much that you can't help smiling, your chest swells, and you could cry from how good it feels.

78
00:04:31,964 --> 00:04:33,260
It's not homework.

79
00:04:33,460 --> 00:04:35,044
You do it because it's fun.

80
00:04:35,594 --> 00:04:39,302
And when you're done imagining, you still do what you need to do.

81
00:04:39,502 --> 00:04:44,182
Calmly, steadily, you live your real life.

82
00:04:44,382 --> 00:04:49,242
That's the difference between someone forcing belief and someone imagining joyfully.

83
00:04:49,442 --> 00:04:51,494
One wears themselves out trying.

84
00:04:51,694 --> 00:04:55,006
The other moves through life already feeling full.

85
00:04:56,156 --> 00:04:58,748
Of course, you might feel afraid.

86
00:04:58,948 --> 00:05:00,820
That feeling is valid too.

87
00:05:01,020 --> 00:05:04,908
But whatever you don't want, try not to dwell on it.

88
00:05:05,458 --> 00:05:12,658
A thought becomes an image, and the deeper the feeling you pour into that image, the more likely it is to be created.

89
00:05:12,858 --> 00:05:16,782
Ever notice how the thing you worried about seemed to happen faster?

90
00:05:16,982 --> 00:05:19,826
That's because we imagine our fears far more vividly.

91
00:05:20,376 --> 00:05:23,148
Feel the fear, but don't give it wings.

92
00:05:23,348 --> 00:05:25,616
Give those wings to what you want.

93
00:05:26,766 --> 00:05:31,086
And most importantly, keep a light heart underneath it all.

94
00:05:31,636 --> 00:05:36,388
From a higher, wider, deeper view, it's okay however it turns out.

95
00:05:36,588 --> 00:05:38,892
Everything is experience.

96
00:05:39,442 --> 00:05:43,366
Things come not when you're desperately clutching, but when you're light.

97
00:05:43,566 --> 00:05:50,874
Keep that it's-okay-either-way feeling underneath, imagine joyfully, live your real life, and keep practicing.

98
00:05:52,024 --> 00:05:55,660
So starting today, try just three things.

99
00:05:56,210 --> 00:05:58,766
One, five minutes before bed.

100
00:05:58,966 --> 00:06:05,950
Breathe deeply until you feel still, then joyfully imagine a day where you already have what you want.

101
00:06:06,150 --> 00:06:08,382
If you smile, that's enough.

102
00:06:08,932 --> 00:06:12,892
Two, when someone compliments you, don't deflect.

103
00:06:13,092 --> 00:06:14,748
Just say, thank you.

104
00:06:14,948 --> 00:06:17,180
It opens your vessel to receive.

105
00:06:17,730 --> 00:06:22,734
Three, whenever money comes in, and whenever it goes out, say thank you.

106
00:06:22,934 --> 00:06:28,586
Gratitude is the feeling of already having, so it shifts the vibration of lack faster than anything.

107
00:06:29,736 --> 00:06:33,300
So let's take one minute together, right now.

108
00:06:33,850 --> 00:06:36,406
Sit comfortably and close your eyes.

109
00:06:39,956 --> 00:06:41,612
Breathe in slowly…

110
00:06:45,812 --> 00:06:48,008
and breathe out, long.

111
00:06:53,558 --> 00:06:54,494
Once more.

112
00:06:54,694 --> 00:06:56,350
Breathe in slowly…

113
00:07:00,550 --> 00:07:02,746
and breathe out, long.

114
00:07:08,296 --> 00:07:09,736
Think of one thing you want.

115
00:07:15,286 --> 00:07:18,382
Now imagine a day where you already have it.

116
00:07:23,932 --> 00:07:25,048
Where do you wake up?

117
00:07:30,598 --> 00:07:32,110
What do you see outside the window?

118
00:07:37,660 --> 00:07:40,216
Who do you meet today, and what do you talk about?

119
00:07:45,766 --> 00:07:48,970
If a smile spreads across your face, that's enough.

120
00:07:52,520 --> 00:07:54,932
Now, take a deep breath in…

121
00:07:59,132 --> 00:08:02,768
and as you slowly breathe out, open your eyes.

122
00:08:06,918 --> 00:08:09,726
Working hard isn't enough on its own.

123
00:08:09,926 --> 00:08:11,402
But neither is imagining.

124
00:08:11,952 --> 00:08:16,668
Open your vessel, imagine joyfully, and live today well.

125
00:08:16,868 --> 00:08:22,052
And underneath it all, a light heart that says it's okay either way.

126
00:08:22,602 --> 00:08:23,898
Money isn't the goal.

127
00:08:24,098 --> 00:08:27,446
It's a tool for the experiences your soul wants to have.

128
00:08:27,996 --> 00:08:29,940
Don't force yourself to believe.

129
00:08:30,140 --> 00:08:31,868
Imagine joyfully.

130
00:08:32,418 --> 00:08:37,062
But even when you do all this, there can be a season where nothing seems to work.

131
00:08:37,262 --> 00:08:41,654
That may not be failure, but a time your soul chose.

132
00:08:41,854 --> 00:08:44,338
I'll talk about that in the next video.

133
00:08:44,888 --> 00:08:48,848
Write one thing you want to joyfully imagine in the comments.

134
00:08:49,048 --> 00:08:51,604
The moment you write it, it's already begun.

135
00:08:52,154 --> 00:08:53,342
Play your own game.
